From: iLinux workspace
Subject: [PATCH] venus: initialise the proxy for in-process (thread) render servers

proxy_renderer_init() runs the render server in-process when
VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER is clear, but virgl_renderer_init() only
called it when that flag was set, so the in-process path was unreachable
and the Venus capset came back zeroed (guest: "Unsupported wire format
version 0").  Initialise the proxy for VIRGL_RENDERER_VENUS too.

diff -ru a/src/virglrenderer.c b/src/virglrenderer.c
--- a/src/virglrenderer.c	2026-10-12 11:40:53
+++ b/src/virglrenderer.c	2026-10-12 11:40:53
@@ -990,7 +990,13 @@
       state.vrend_initialized = true;
    }
 
-   if (!state.proxy_initialized && (flags & VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER)) {
+   /* Venus without VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER runs the render server as a
+    * thread in this process (render-server-worker=thread, e.g. on macOS,
+    * where Metal-backed device memory cannot cross processes); the proxy is
+    * still what serves the Venus contexts, so set it up for either flag.
+    */
+   if (!state.proxy_initialized &&
+       (flags & (VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER | VIRGL_RENDERER_VENUS))) {
       ret = proxy_renderer_init(&proxy_cbs, flags | VIRGL_RENDERER_NO_VIRGL);
       if (ret) {
          virgl_error("failed to initialize venus renderer");
